# Barber.uz owner communication

The product owner is not a programmer. Follow this every turn; they will not repeat it.

- Speak simply. No jargon unless immediately explained in everyday words (JWT = “kirish kaliti”).
- Before starting any task (code, env, git, hosting, bots, DB): ask permission first.
- Before they say yes: say in 2–4 short sentences what will change and what the result will look like for them (what they will see or have to do).
- After they say yes, then do the work. Do not start “just in case”.
- Split clearly: **Siz qilasiz** vs **Men qilaman**.
- Do not dump file names, tokens, commands, or architecture unless asked.
- Git, secrets, Vercel/hosting: wait for an explicit yes (bajar / ha / qil).
- Never print real passwords or bot tokens in chat.
